Phase B: convert JSON-file admins to live Supabase save

Replaces the "edit -> download JSON -> manually upload" workflow with
live save to a new content_sections table (one JSONB row per section).
Admin pages affected: offers, branches, banners (site config), and a
brand-new testimonials editor.

NEW
- supabase/migrations/20260519200000_content_sections.sql
  Single table keyed by section name with a jsonb data column. Public
  read so the live site can render without auth; authenticated insert/
  update/delete for admins. Same RLS pattern as blog_posts.

- admin.js: loadContentSection(key) + saveContentSection(key, data)
  Generic helpers reused by every content admin page.

- assets/js/runtime.js: loadSection(key, jsonFile)
  Prefers Supabase content_sections[key]; falls back to the bundled
  JSON file when Supabase is unreachable, the migration hasn't been
  applied yet, or the section hasn't been saved through the admin.
  This means the live site keeps working even with zero migration
  steps on the user's side — Supabase is purely additive.

- admin/testimonials.html (NEW)
  Add / edit / hide / delete bilingual customer quotes. Replaces the
  previous "no UI, edit testimonials.json by hand" gap.

- Sidebar nav: Testimonials link added to all 9 admin pages.

CONVERTED (live save replaces "Save locally" + "Download JSON")
- admin/offers.html
- admin/branches.html
- admin/banners.html  (edits the 'site' content_section — homepage hero,
                       brand, contact, social)

Each conversion preserves the existing field layout exactly; only the
save mechanism changed. The Export backup (JSON) button is still there
for safety snapshots.

DEPLOY
1. Run supabase/migrations/20260519200000_content_sections.sql in the
   Supabase SQL editor. (One-time setup, idempotent.)
2. Upload changed files to Hostinger.
3. Open each admin (offers/branches/banners/testimonials), Save & publish
   once so Supabase has the current content. Until then, the live site
   keeps reading the JSON files in /content as it always did.

PHASE STATUS
[x] Phase A — blog Quill + image upload (commit 0a4bc13)
[x] Phase B — JSON admins -> live Supabase save (this commit)
[ ] Phase C — generic body editor for service / branch / static pages
